  "body": "Found while fixing #1536.\n\n#1536 (PR to follow) wraps each STEP face's surface in a metered surface (`crates/app/src/geometry/import/step_guard.rs`). B-spline and NURBS face divisions now stop at `FACE_EVAL_CAP` evaluations, and the import is refused by name. Two kinds of division are still unmetered:\n\n- **Edge curves.** `cshell_tessellation` divides each edge with `PolylineCurve::from_curve`, which runs truck's recursive curve `parameter_division`. A discontinuous B-spline or NURBS edge curve (an interior knot repeated past its degree) has the same shape as the #1536 loop, and nothing bounds it.\n- **Swept surfaces** (`Surface::SweptCurve`: extrusions and revolutions of a `Curve3D`). Their division goes through the swept curve's division, which is also unmetered.\n\nNo file that hangs this way is known yet. This is the remaining gap in the \"no input file can hang the importer\" promise.\n\nDone means: a STEP whose edge curve (and one whose swept surface) is a discontinuous B-spline is refused by name inside a hard time limit, pinned like `import_step_guard`. Normal imports must stay byte-identical (the division algorithm is unchanged, only metered).\n",
